														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2190364">
									

<p>I originally had it as SCP-2240-1 and SCP-2240-2 throughout, but (and this is my fault) I ended up referencing them way too often, and seeing SCP-2240-1 and SCP-2240-2 repeated ad nauseam looked bad. I asked in #site19 and someone said it'd be fine to abbreviate to -1 and -2 for multiple uses in the same paragraph.</p>
<p>The dialogue is coming from a twenty-something South Floridian pill head who as far as he knows got transferred from one jail to a better jail because of his boyfriend (who may be a bona fide ghost or may just be the hallucination of a delusional and untalented reality bender.) I thought the dialogue was appropriate for that. I was going to add a Site Director note at one point, but TwistedGears in #site19 persuaded me that it was too on-the-nail about the concept. Though the finished version might actually have gone a bit far in the other direction&#8230;</p>

							</div>

								
