														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2190373">
									

<p>Hm. I'm not really sure.</p>
<p>The concept's all right. Tone, writing, procedures, and description is pretty good for a first skip. The concept is weird, but it doesn't make me really that confused or creeped out, which I personally feel can be done better with an idea like this.</p>
<p>I am novoting, though, just because of two things that can't make me up vote. One is 2240-2's description, which could be really creative but it just feels rushed and glossed over. It's very easy to say, 'spatial anomaly that we can barely detect' but I dunno, is that all? Maybe adding more info to the nature of 2240-2 could give this article a little more flesh on its bones, which it needs.</p>
<p>Second is the interview. I understand the guy is supposed to be obtuse, but what does it really add to the article other than a few &quot;lol we're gay&quot; jokes? I mean, yeah, he says he sees his boyfriend, he says medicine didn't work, but what can you add that really sells the article?</p>
<p>As for usage of -1 and -2, just use SCP-2240-1 and SCP-2240-2. People will more likely downvote for usage of the former than redundancy of the latter.</p>

							</div>

								
					
