			<div class="content" id="post-content-2190407">
									

<p>&quot;as well as four (4) bruised bite marks to the left side of the neck, regarding which SCP-2240-1 has not been forthcoming.&quot; XD</p>
<p>Too bad it doesn't really go anywhere, cuz I think it's kinda sweet. For some ideas &#8212; plenty of non-invasive tests into -2's range are possible, stupid things like seeing how far away they can put the water cooler and still have him get -1 a drink for example. Some of the standard ESP tests might be interesting too &#8212; have -2 see the cards, but -1 not, and have -1 answer what's on them (there's a set of cards somebody made for this, but I can't remember wtf they're called).</p>
<p>The other thing you could do would be to take gay stereotypes and turn them on their head, but idk how well that could be worked into a clinical tone.</p>
<p>No vote, because I do like it, but think you could do more with it.</p>
<p>Edit: you could also play up the psych aspect &#8212; how glad he is to be believed instead of dosed with anti-psychotics (some of which can have some <em>nasty</em> side effects you could maybe use).</p>
<p>As usual, thedeadlymoose nailed it. This is a person, haunted by his dead lover, getting to continue that relationship after death, who's been on all sorts of drugs, arrested, thought crazy (by himself even); there's so much here to work with, but he feels like a cardboard cutout, not a person.</p>
<p>Also, the note reads like lolFoundation. We got that they're hickeys, no need to spell it out.</p>

							</div>

								
