			<div class="content" id="post-content-2330715">
									

<p>Overall, I like it. The concept is nice, not creepy/squicky, but very human/psychological. The character is a little wooden, but not unbelievable. I've got a couple of questions:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2240-2 is a spacetime anomaly of an as yet undetermined nature, completely imperceptible by all non-anomalous Foundation technology&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So have we considered any more anomalous options? I know cross-testing is discouraged, but there have been references in tales to Foundation-developed anomalous technology. I think determining whether or not it <em>has</em> a form is something that we'd want to know.</p>
<p>Why haven't we done a relayed interview with -2? I got the impression that -2 can &quot;hear&quot; what the Foundation researchers are saying; why haven't we done more with this? It's understood that the information would be suspect, but could be used to help determine if -1 is suffering the stresses of having to lie on the fly. Hell, hook him up to a polygraph. &quot;Tell us something SCP-2240-1 wouldn't know.&quot; <em>Color drains out of SCP-2240-1s face. He then proceeds to get very angry.</em> They are observed 'fighting' for a period of ?? days, before reconciliation.&quot;</p>
<p>The tests mentioned above by Argenti make sense. Range of effect (or lack of a definable range) would be cool to know.</p>
<p>Just my .02. +1 for concept, hoping it becomes all it can be.</p>

